{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1474334-tremere-weakness","id":1474334,"title":"Tremere weakness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-09T16:40:34-08:00","id":1474334,"title":"Tremere weakness","content":"I was trying to rectify different versions of the tremere weakness and figure out something that actually makes sense with their background and I think I came up with something. <br /> <br /> Tremere are not actually kindred, or rather, most of them are not. The council of seven and their peers are actually kindred, but everyone else is something very kindred-like whose creation is not completed until they preform the tremere oath and creation rites and drink the blood of one or more of the original seven.<br /> <br /> In essence, each tremere not only is one step bound to the pyramid, but they cannot sire except through that binding, their childer's embrace failing some number of days to hours later if the blood of an actual kindred isn't imbibed within that time.<br /> <br /> Sabbat propaganda is real and they are actually fake vampires that can only pretend to the curse of caine with actual cainite (or settite) blood in their veins.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, I wanted to know what people here thought of that or if it seriously messes with lore in some way I'm not familiar with or if there are other ideas on how to fix this broken curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T20:09:08-08:00","id":1474348,"title":"","content":"I think Lasombra\u2019s new technology allergy fits better with Tremere with the rationalization that they have become so focused and dependent on magic that science is starting to evade their grasp. It makes sense that they would still be so focused on magic 50 years into the Space Age, with instant communication and self driving cars, if those options were more and more limited for them. It also fits well with the Camarilla\u2019s new ban on electronic communications. Tremere would be working to encourage that to downplay their own weakness while increasing their utility.<br /> <br /> (As for Lasombra, I think that if No Reflection isn\u2019t bad enough in it\u2019s own, adding Deep Sleeper to it fits the clan better than tech issues. Limit dice pools to awaken and to function during the day. The sun weighs heavier on the clan of shadow.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24351-garygeneric","name":"Garygeneric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T23:08:53-08:00","id":1474416,"title":"","content":"Tremere have no weakness because they're the best clan ever. <br /> <br /> To be more serious, from a purely sociological point of view, the point of a clan Weakness is to bring that clan together. Having the same strengths (IE Disciplines) for the most part makes bloodlines their own biggest competitors: A Nosferatu and a Ventrue have a lot to gain from working with eachother and they naturally feed in different areas so there's little reason to fight eachother, but without the weakness A Nosferatu sees another Nosferatu as a competitor that devalues his trade, and a Ventrue sees another ventrue who's after his background dots. Weaknesses force clans like the Nosferatu to work together, while the Ventrue weakness is doubly genius in that Ventrue probably won't have the same food type and thus have a lot of reasons to cooperate (he can find food for me and I can find food for him, we can both target the food source of a traitor...) <br /> <br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy takes a lot of time to master which takes away from the time a vampire can acquire the means to defend himself and his coveted works. The Tremere weakness WORKS because Thaumaturges really have two strategies to practice their craft in security: The first is secrecy, a chosen by Assamite Sorcerers and Settites, and the second is dependence on a large backer. (obviously, they're not mutually exclusive; the As/FoS Sorcerers are attached to organization, and the Tremere are secretive, but they certainly have leanings) <br /> <br /> If a Tremere who wishes to invest in magic can't abide the Pyramid or become an integral part to a coterie/pack/anarch gang their next best choice is to become a pocket wizard in service to some powerful vampire with the means to look after the Tremere thaumaturge while he masters his spells. A Tremere essentially needs to submit to others, so easier blood bonds is really rather fitting for them. Thaumaturgy is best a service you can provide to others: it's natural. <br /> <br /> *yes, a Tremere can manage it alone by using Dominate 4 or bloodbonds and surrounding himself with goons, but that's just Pyramid 2, and this strategy isn't good for low level Tremere and most coteries can bulldoze through such defences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T08:54:41-08:00","id":1474431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1474334-tremere-weakness?p=1474416#post1474416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere have no weakness because they're the best clan ever.<br /> <br /> To be more serious, from a purely sociological point of view, the point of a clan Weakness is to bring that clan together. Having the same strengths (IE Disciplines) for the most part makes bloodlines their own biggest competitors: A Nosferatu and a Ventrue have a lot to gain from working with eachother and they naturally feed in different areas so there's little reason to fight eachother, but without the weakness A Nosferatu sees another Nosferatu as a competitor that devalues his trade, and a Ventrue sees another ventrue who's after his background dots. Weaknesses force clans like the Nosferatu to work together, while the Ventrue weakness is doubly genius in that Ventrue probably won't have the same food type and thus have a lot of reasons to cooperate (he can find food for me and I can find food for him, we can both target the food source of a traitor...)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the bigger reason the weakness forces Ventrue to work together is that all Ventrue need a stable herd, so no Ventrue wants chaos. A chaotic city is a city where your herd will either be dead or in hiding, and no Ventrue can just switch to whatever happens to be available.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T11:40:39-08:00","id":1475051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1474334-tremere-weakness#post1474334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, I wanted to know what people here thought of that or if it seriously messes with lore in some way I'm not familiar with or if there are other ideas on how to fix this broken curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't seriously messes with anything. They really aren't Cainites anyway, so your theory works fine.<br /> <br /> If you use the forum's search engine you'll find a good number of threads full with ideas for the Tremere weakness, it is the weakness with most houserules along with Ravnos'. Making Thaumaturgy Out-of-Clan (so they have only two in-clans), making them addicted to magic, making rules for the Pyramid's interference, and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}